criu restore capability, measured 2026-07-31
aarch64, Docker Desktop VM kernel 6.12, --privileged.

Product-free probe: a plain C program printing a line every 20ms, dumped with
`criu dump -t <pid> --shell-job`, then restored. No reproit in the picture.
Run with `--restore-detached` (A) and without it (B). "lines" is the subject's
own output before the restore and 3s after it.

== debian:trixie, criu 4.1.1 ==
Version: 4.1.1
== A: with --restore-detached ==
  dump: OK
  restore [A --restore-detached]: exit=137 elapsed=30s
  lines: 88 -> 88
== B: without --restore-detached ==
  dump: OK
  restore [B ]: exit=137 elapsed=30s
  lines: 87 -> 87

== debian:bookworm, criu 3.17.1 ==
Version: 3.17.1
== A: with --restore-detached ==
  dump: OK
  restore [A --restore-detached]: exit=0 elapsed=0s
  lines: 87 -> 216
== B: without --restore-detached ==
  dump: OK
  restore [B ]: exit=137 elapsed=30s
  lines: 88 -> 1371

exit=137 is SIGKILL from a 30s `timeout -s KILL`: criu 4.1.1 does not return,
and SIGTERM alone did not end it. In B on 3.17.1 criu stays in the foreground
holding the restored tree, which is why it is also killed at 30s, but its tail
advanced 88 -> 1371, so the restore itself worked. The dump succeeds on both
versions; only restore differs.

CONCLUSION: criu 4.1.1 cannot restore on this host and criu 3.17.1 can. The
checkpoint acceptance therefore requires a bookworm based image. The reproit
binary must be built against that same image: a trixie built binary needs
GLIBC_2.39 and dies at exec on bookworm.

Product behavior under the hang, which is correct and unchanged: it bounds the
wait and refuses rather than guessing.
  {"verdict": "inconclusive", "exit": 3, "outcome": "stale",
   "reason": "criu restore did not return within 120s"}

Green run of validation/process-checkpoint/run.sh on bookworm with criu
3.17.1, using a bookworm built binary:
  captured 802 boundary entries over 400 iterations
  replay from zero: 2878 ms, verdict=reproduced, exit=1
  anchored after 350 lines of the subject's own output
  restore: verdict=inconclusive exit=3
  tail resumed from 356 to 400 lines of the subject's own output
  MEASURED: full replay 2878 ms for 400 iterations;
            the anchor skipped the first 356 of them
  7 of 7 cases, script exit=0
